  "id": "COMPOUND:41991 - PROTEIN:3786",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential mechanism by which the compound [(5R,6R,8R,9S,10R,13R,14S,15S,17R)-17-[(1S)-1-[(2R)-4,5-dimethyl-6-oxo-2,3-dihydropyran-2-yl]ethyl]-5,6,14-trihydroxy-10,13-dimethyl-1-oxo-4,6,7,8,9,11,12,15,16,17-decahydrocyclopenta[a]phenanthren-15-yl] acetate interacts with the Tubulin beta-2A chain. This compound is identified as a target of Phytolaccoside B, which is itself a target of several kinases, including Mitogen-activated protein kinase kinase kinase kinase 2, Serine/threonine-protein kinase ULK2, and Tyrosine-protein kinase CSK. These kinases are involved in various cellular processes, including cell survival, proliferation, and signaling pathways that are critical for maintaining cellular homeostasis. The observed interaction between the compound and the Tubulin beta-2A chain implies that Phytolaccoside B may exert its effects through the modulation of these kinases, potentially influencing the function of the Tubulin beta-2A chain. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between the compound and the Tubulin beta-2A chain, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
